.TH APER 1 "July 28, 2026" "aper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aper \- render and serialise substitution-tiling systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aper
.RB [ \-L " directory" ]
.RB [ \-t " type" " | " \-f " file" ]
.RB [ \-s " seed" ]
.RB [ \-c " scheme" ]
.RB [ \-n " depth" ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.br
.B aper
.RB [ \-L " directory" ]
.RB [ \-t " type" " | " \-f " file" ]
.B \--definition
.br
.BR aper " " { \-h | \-\-help }
.br
.BR aper " " { \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aper
generates either a clipped substitution-tiling patch or a sheet showing every
prototile replacement, and writes a complete native vector PDF to standard
output.  Systems may be selected from a rule library and its built-in
fallbacks, or read from one declarative file containing polygonal prototiles,
similarities, rules, and seeds.  A selected system may instead be written in
normalised declarative form.
Diagnostics are written to standard error, so the PDF can be redirected or
piped without contamination.
.PP
Declarative systems are checked for structural and area consistency, simple
parent polygons, containment, overlap, gaps, and matching internal edges before
they are rendered.  Version 1 covers finite planar polygon substitutions with
a scalar inflation and rotated or reflected similarities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tiling " " type
Select a system by identifier or alias from the composed rule library.
The six legacy built-in systems are
.B p1
for three pentagon types, a diamond, a boat, and a star,
.B p2
for kite-and-dart tiles,
.B p3
for thin and thick Penrose rhombs,
.B ammann-beenker
for squares and 45-degree rhombs,
.B pinwheel
for right triangles,
.B stampfli
for the three-tile 12-fold 1 rule.
The distributed declarative library adds
.B thue-morse-2d
for complementary binary square blocks,
.B chair
for the L-triomino rep-tile,
.B domino
for the table tiling,
.BR square-chair ,
.BR squiral-block ,
.BR period-tripling-2d ,
.BR pentomino ,
.BR tromino1 ,
and
.BR tromino2 .
The descriptive aliases
.BR pentagon-boat-star ,
.BR kite-dart ,
and
.BR rhomb ,
plus the short aliases
.B ab
and
.BR stampfli-12-fold-1 ,
and the
.B thue-morse
alias are also accepted.
The default is
.BR p3 .
Definitions loaded with
.B \--library
may provide additional identifiers and aliases.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " file
Read one declarative
.B .aper
system instead of selecting a library system.
A file contains named polygonal prototiles, an inflation, one replacement per
type, and named seeds.
Use
.B \-
to read standard input.
This option may not be combined with
.B \--tiling
or
.BR \--library .
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-library " " directory
Recursively load every
.B .aper
definition below
.IR directory ,
then add the built-in catalogue as fallbacks.
Without this option, aper first tries
.I ./rules
and, when that directory is absent, the installed
.I PREFIX/share/aper/rules
library.
A file definition with a built-in identifier must describe the same canonical
rule, and a library alias may not shadow a built-in identifier.
This option may not be combined with
.BR \--file .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seed " " seed
Select the patch's starting design.
P1 provides
.BR pentagon-5 ,
.BR pentagon-3 ,
.BR pentagon-2 ,
.BR diamond ,
.BR boat ,
and
.BR star .
P2 provides
.BR sun ,
.BR star ,
.BR ace ,
.BR deuce ,
.BR jack ,
.BR queen ,
and
.BR king .
P3 provides
.BR sun ,
.BR star ,
.BR thin ,
and
.BR thick .
Ammann-Beenker provides
.BR octagon ,
.BR square ,
and
.BR rhomb .
Pinwheel provides
.BR triangle .
Stampfli 12-fold 1 provides
.BR dodecagon ,
.BR triangle ,
.BR square ,
and
.BR rhomb .
Thue-Morse 2D provides
.B a
and
.BR b .
Chair and Domino each provide a seed with the same name as the system.
P1 defaults to
.BR pentagon-5 ;
P2 and P3 default to
.BR sun ;
Ammann-Beenker defaults to
.BR octagon ;
Pinwheel defaults to
.BR triangle ;
Stampfli 12-fold 1 defaults to
.BR dodecagon ;
and Thue-Morse 2D defaults to
.BR a .
Chair and Domino default to their eponymous seeds.
Library and file-defined systems declare their own default.
The P3
.B thin
seed requires a depth of at least 2.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-colour " " scheme
Select one of the
.BR flare ,
.BR grove ,
.BR electric ,
or
.B tide
colour schemes.
The default is
.BR flare .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-depth " " depth
Set the number of patch substitutions.
P1 accepts an integer from 1 through 6 and defaults to 5.
P2 and P3 accept an integer from 1 through 12 and default to 7.
Ammann-Beenker accepts 1 through 6 and defaults to 4.
Pinwheel accepts 1 through 8 and defaults to 6.
Stampfli 12-fold 1 accepts 1 through 3 and defaults to 2.
Thue-Morse 2D accepts 1 through 7 and defaults to 4.
Chair and Domino accept 1 through 8 and default to 5.
Library and file-defined systems declare their own range.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule
Render a sheet containing every prototile and its one-step substitution
instead of a finite patch.
The tiling and colour options still apply.
The seed and depth options may not be used with rule output.
.TP
.B \--definition
Write the selected system as normalised
.B .aper
text instead of PDF.
The tiling, file, and library selection options still apply.
The rule, seed, and depth options may not be used with definition output.
Some legacy built-in systems depend on construction pieces or presentation
projectors that the version 1 format cannot reproduce exactly.  Such a system
is rejected instead of being written with changed semantics.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a concise help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render the default tiling and open it:
.PP
.EX
aper > tiling.pdf
open tiling.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render a P1 pentagon-5 patch using the flare colour scheme:
.PP
.EX
aper -t p1 -s pentagon-5 -c flare -n 5 > p1.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render a P2 queen patch using the electric colour scheme:
.PP
.EX
aper -t p2 -s queen -c electric -n 5 > queen.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render a Stampfli 12-fold 1 patch:
.PP
.EX
aper -t stampfli -c flare -n 2 > stampfli.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render the Pinwheel substitution rule:
.PP
.EX
aper -t pinwheel --rule -c tide > pinwheel-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render the two-dimensional Thue-Morse rule:
.PP
.EX
aper -t thue-morse-2d --rule > thue-morse-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Render a system supplied entirely as data:
.PP
.EX
aper --file rules/chair.aper -n 5 > chair.pdf
aper --file rules/chair.aper --rule > chair-rule.pdf
.EE
.PP
Select a data-defined rule by identifier, then serialise it deterministically:
.PP
.EX
aper --library rules --tiling square-chair --rule > square-chair-rule.pdf
aper --file rules/chair.aper --definition > chair-copy.aper
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./rules
First default recursively searched rule-library directory when it exists.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/aper/rules
Installed fallback rule-library directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B aper
exits zero after writing a complete PDF document or declarative definition and
non-zero if its arguments are invalid, a definition cannot be loaded, or
output fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aper-search (1)
